respondent Amanda Walker reports it  doesn't look like much but a bridge just  beyond this checkpoint could provide a  pivotal moment for the people of  Venezuela US aid is on its way here to  Colombia getting it across the border is  a sensitive and secretive mission from  local farmland you can see a barrier in  the middle of the bridge recently put  there by President Maduro soldiers  Dianna's farm overlooks what could  become a flashpoint in this crisis what  do you think might happen on the bridge  [Music]  the people is gonna come and they're  gonna take it away do what they need to  do Colombia clearly wants this aid to  get through that's why later they allow  a small group of TV news cameras  including our own to seema Doros  makeshift blockade up close the  embattled leaders message is clear he  does not want international aid entering  his country Venezuela 'he's other  proclaimed leader Hwang Guido says it  needs to come now every day up to 30,000  people cross this other public bridge  from Venezuela into Colombia some are  leaving for good for most people it's a  daily grueling shopping trip for  necessities they can't get at home some  have walked miles in the baking heat  they're using what little money they  have four basic food pain relief nappies  and a few extras to sweeten an  incredibly tough existence Maria makes  the crossing every day with her five  children her main concern is the total  absence of medical facilities in  Venezuela there was nothing in there I  have to come here and get help my  daughter collapsed yesterday and I have  to come to the Red Cross in Colombia  she says her neighbor's son just died of  malnutrition like millions of Venezuelan  mothers she is doing everything she  possibly can  to protect her own people are also  selling whatever they can to scratch a  living desperate times call for  desperate measures this vendor is asking  women if they want to sell their hair  and if they're willing to sell this  length they could get up to $10 which in  this climate can make a big difference  everyone here has become adept at  finding things to make life bearable but  people need so much more than they can  get here they need proper aid Anna's  Whelan's have been carrying a heavy load  for years now this way of life isn't new  what has changed is a feeling of hope  help is at least on the horizon Amanda  Walker sky news cúcuta Columbia
 

